// The return clause of a `native` declaration, and its node. The clause is
// checked token by token: a body written where none belongs would otherwise
// be read as a return type.

native_ret(int[] pos, string name, int[] params) {
  expect_text(pos, "return");
  advance(pos);
  int ret_i = native_type(pos, name, params);
} return int ret_i;
given decl_tokens ([33], "nm1", []):(0) then prints:("<stdin>:1: error: expected ';', found 's' [E0101]\n  at: s\n  why: the grammar needs ';' here to finish what it was reading, so the construct before this point is incomplete or mistyped\n  help: put ';' where it belongs; if it looks right, check the line before for a missing ';', ')' or '}', because those are noticed one token late\n")
